WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.350
Take one word from the Bible: Jerusalem.

2
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.450
A medieval reader could
find four meanings in it:

3
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:10.180
a city, the Church, the soul, and heaven.

4
00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.350
Today, one Christian reads
Genesis 1 as exact history.

5
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.350
Another reads the same
chapter quite differently.

6
00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.060
If Christians agree the
Bible is God's word,

7
00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:23.580
why do they read the same
verse in such different ways?

8
00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.620
In this mission, you'll meet
the old senses of scripture,

9
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.460
and two twentieth-century
theologians, Barth and Bultmann,

10
00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:31.760
who rethought them.

11
00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:36.450
Then you'll map a range of views,
from fundamentalism to liberalism.

12
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.270
Your mission: find out why Christians who
agree the Bible is God's word read the

13
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.150
same verse so differently.
